{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And there were twelve springs of water and seventy palm trees</b> — it is not a great matter that seventy palm trees be found in a place, for in low-lying places one may find a thousand palm trees and more than that, and many springs of water flow out in valleys and in the mountains, and the verse would not report this. Rabbi Abraham Ibn Ezra said (commentary on Exodus 15:27) that the verse reports that they came to a good place, the opposite of Marah, for in Elim there are many springs and they are sweet and beautiful waters, since palm trees do not thrive in land whose waters are bitter, and therefore it says <b>\"and they encamped there\"</b>, for they tarried there on account of this for more days than the other stations through which they passed. But in the section of These Are the Stages, it reports nothing about the waters of Marah, and says: \"And they journeyed from Marah and came to Elim, and there were twelve springs of water and seventy palm trees, and they encamped there\" (Numbers 33:9), and it did not elaborate thus for all the stations of the journey.\n\nAnd Rashi wrote (commentary on Exodus 15:27): <b>Twelve springs of water</b> — corresponding to the twelve tribes they were prepared for them. <b>And seventy palm trees</b> — corresponding to the seventy elders. I do not know what this preparation is, if it was done through a miracle at that moment. But I saw in the Mekhilta (ad loc.): Rabbi Elazar HaModa'i said: From the day the Holy One, blessed be He, created His world, He created there twelve springs corresponding to the twelve tribes of Israel, and seventy palm trees corresponding to the seventy elders. And the verse reports this because they encamped upon them, each tribe at its spring, and the elders sat in their shade, to praise El over them, that He had prepared thus for them in a dry land. And furthermore, our Rabbis in the midrash of Rabbi Nechunya ben HaKanah on this verse gave a wondrous interpretation in our eyes:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:08:56.537924297Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}